{number: 43}
{title: Rock of Ages, Cleft for Me}
{key: Bb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Bb] Rock of Ages, cleft for me,
Let me [Eb] hide my-[Bb] self in [F7] Thee;
Let the [Bb] water and the blood,
From Thy [Eb] wounded [Bb] side which [F7] flowed,
Be of [Bb] sin the double cure,
Save from [Eb] wrath and [Bb] make [F7] me [Bb] pure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Bb] Could my tears forever flow,
Could my [Eb] zeal no [Bb] languor [F7] know,
These for [Bb] sin could not atone;
Thou must [Eb] save, and [Bb] Thou a-[F7] lone:
In my [Bb] hand no price I bring,
Simply [Eb] to Thy [Bb] cross [F7] I [Bb] cling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Bb] While I draw this fleeting breath,
When my [Eb] eyes shall [Bb] close in [F7] death,
When I [Bb] rise to worlds unknown,
And be-[Eb] hold Thee [Bb] on Thy [F7] throne,
Rock of [Bb] Ages, cleft for me,
Let me [Eb] hide my-[Bb] self in [F7] Thee. [Bb]
{end_of_verse}
